            'question' => 'What is the INR test and why is it important?',
            'answer' => 'INR (International Normalized Ratio) is a standardized blood test that measures how fast your blood clots. For most patients on warfarin, the target INR is 2.0 to 3.0. If it is too low, you are at risk of clots; if it is too high, you are at risk of bleeding.',
